				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Enforce explicit Fn path for ExtensionInstall\n\nUpdate the import in `ExtensionInstall.rs` to use the fully qualified path `UriComponents::FromFilePath::Fn` instead of the module alias `UriFromFilePath`.\n\nThis change aligns the extension installation handler with the project's strict `Struct::Struct` and `Fn` naming conventions, ensuring all function calls are explicit and removing implicit module re-exports. This maintains consistency with recent refactoring efforts in `FileRealpath` and other IPC handlers that migrate inline types and functions to dedicated PascalCase modules, reducing ambiguity in the Wind service handler layer.",
			"SHA": "40e5b9780834547f1338ff3c4a23c7b42ec4abff"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:05:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1137,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Atomize RecoverState into dedicated PascalCase modules\n\nDecompose the 177-line `RecoverState.rs` monolith into a directory of focused modules (`ValidateAndCleanState`, `SafeStateOperationWithTimeout`, `RecoverStateWithBackoff`) to enforce the project's `Struct::Struct` and `Fn` naming conventions. The original file contained three distinct recovery primitives: predicate-driven map filtering, off-thread blocking operations with timeout, and async retry with exponential backoff.\n\nThese utilities are now exposed as individual module files with a clear \"one export per file\" identity, aligning with recent architectural shifts seen in `MementoLoader` and `FileRealpath`. The parent file now serves strictly as a barrel export and architectural documentation, clarifying the separation between validation, timeout handling, and backoff logic while awaiting formal integration into the `ApplicationState` recovery flow.",
			"SHA": "6d642b4185fabe075f5b5494b534ca4b97974a19"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:04:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1137,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Atomize MementoLoader into dedicated function modules\n\nDecompose the 190-line `MementoLoader.rs` monolith into a directory of focused PascalCase modules (`LoadInitialMementoFromDisk`, `LoadMementoWithRecovery`, `AttemptMementoRecovery`, `CreateCorruptedBackup`) to enforce the project's `Struct::Struct` and `Fn` naming conventions.\n\nThe original file contained logic for best-effort loading, recovery flows, and timestamped backup creation. These are now exposed as individual module files with a clear \"one export per file\" identity, aligning with the architectural shift seen in recent commits (`RecoverState`). The file itself now serves as a barrel export and architectural documentation, clarifying the separation between the best-effort `default()` loader and the error-propagating recovery loader.\n\nThis change prepares the persistence layer for cleaner dependency injection from `Environment::StorageProvider` and reduces coupling in the `ApplicationState` boot path.",
			"SHA": "600afe5343df30878c1aaea0f8fd7a9b6be7b7fd"
		}
